SWEET WLAN join / cred / L25 headers (P-W-JOIN, T-4209; verbatim copies, no caller yet, no behaviour change):
adds bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_join.h, sweet_wlan_join_fw.h, sweet_wlan_cred.h, sweet_wlan_l25.h, sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h, sweet_wlan_l25_rsne.h and
sweet_wlan_l25_glue.h as byte-identical copies of the shim/ sources (the host-tested, mutant-checked L24/L25 engines and the glue of T-37d8),
so the kernel glue (T-8573) can include them. Include order (header comment of sweet_wlan_l25_glue.h): data, join, g2, l25, l25_rsne, cred, glue.
Nothing in the tree includes them yet, so the kernel build and every L24/L25 gate are unchanged. shim/build.sh cmp's each hunk against shim/
(xnu patch 0206 == shim/ sources). Not compiled against XNU: join.h and cred.h still include <stdio.h>/<string.h>, which T-8573 must swap for
<sys/systm.h> / <string.h> before the first include (same step patch 0199 did for data.h).

